~ ambushed
Wizard: Well well well. What doth we has't here? A lone pint-size, is't?
Fenn: Why do you call me that? I'm Fenn.
Wizard: Well, Fenn. If't even is thine real nameth. Um... I do not knoweth...
Wizard: Um... well... I hath lost mine own traineth of bethought.
Fenn: Uh...
Wizard: Ah, of course! Ambushing thee!
Wizard: Treadeth carefully, pint-size. T'wouldst such a shame if thee were crushed by mine own creations.
Az: cough Fenn, you good over there?
Wizard: WHAT? WHO IS'T THERE? A GHOSTLY SPIRIT OF MINE OWN IMAGINATION?!
Fenn: I'm good, Az. Wizard man is just ambushing me.
Wizard: AZ? Liketh apprentice Az? Like, like Az Featherstone, Az?
Fenn: Yeah. We're like-eth best friends.
Az: Uh. Sure.
Wizard: Wherefore is the lady? How doth she be talking?
Fenn: Oh! Az made these cool frienship bracelets-
Az: Bangles
Fenn: Bangles. And we can talk through them!
Wizard: No matter! Speaketh not anym're of this curs'd device. This changes't nothing!
Wizard: TAKETH THIS!
=> END


~ escaped
Az: Haha! Nice work, kid!
Wizard: INCONCEIVABLE! ARRRGH!
Wizard: HOW DIDST THOU EVADE MINE OWN ATTACKS?!
Fenn: Oh, well Az can also grab things from far away using these bracelets-
Az: Ban- nevermind.
Wizard: Arrgh. I need to do-eth better! More machines, more snoweth, more creatures.
Az: Yeah. cough. I'm not gonna lie, that was pretty pathetic.
Wizard: Grrr. Well, I doubteth thee has't any more stupid tricks up thy sleeve.
Fenn: Wasn't it so cool?
Wizard: I hath never said it was cool!
Wizard: ARRGH!!!!!
Wizard runs off
=> END
#Should be used for both the pre-ambush conversation and post-ambush conversation
